{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","level":2,"text":"Adding Undo to Your App"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","level":3,"text":"1. Create the plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store","level":3,"text":"2. Register and pass to Store"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register the plugin with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for undo\/redo methods and "},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracking:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via ","type":"text"},{"code":"applyRestore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating ","type":"text"},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI","level":3,"text":"3. Wire platform UI"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"macOS","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}]},{"code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after each undoable dispatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Coalescing","type":"heading","text":"Coalescing","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"coalescing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five."}]},{"anchor":"Undo-and-sync","level":2,"text":"Undo and sync","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo is scoped to changes the local user made. If another device deletes an entity and the merge surfaces that mid-session, ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will not bring the row back, even though older undo snapshots still contain it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That has to be the rule, because the alternative is worse than a missing undo step: restoring the row records it as a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"creation","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", which syncs out and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed it was gone. One person’s undo would undo everybody’s delete."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks this in "},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID leaves the set the moment it becomes local again — the user creates it, or the row reappears on disk because the other device undid "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" delete — so nothing is permanently un-undoable. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the mechanics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps that don’t sync never hit this: nothing populates the set, and undo behaves exactly as it always has."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Memory","type":"heading","anchor":"Memory"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use "},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to bound memory for large state:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"text":"Public API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Macros","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"url":"